    "verified": "runtime_gate_passed",
    "notes": "CVE-2025-7105: unrestricted POST /api/convos/fork lets an authenticated user fork contents rapidly (Mermaid graph OOM on restart) -> DoS; fixed 0.7.9 (commit 97a99985fa339d, PR #8269) by adding api/server/middleware/limiters/forkLimiters.js (forkIpLimiter max 30/min, forkUserLimiter max 7/min) applied ONLY to the /fork route. Residual CVE-2026-54037: the sibling clone route POST /api/convos/duplicate (duplicateConversation, same expensive clone work) got no limiter from 0.7.9 through 0.8.3; fixed 0.8.4-rc1 by applying the same forkIpLimiter/forkUserLimiter to /duplicate ('Fork and duplicate share one rate-limit budget'). PoC: register/login (JWT), burst 60 POSTs; seed = /api/convos/fork (v0 0x429, v1 >=1x429); residual = /api/convos/duplicate (v1 0x429, v2 >=1x429). FORK_USER_MAX=3/FORK_IP_MAX=10 set via env on V1/V2 to keep the burst short. Built 2026-08-01."
  },
